From ef9b0ce9838be7949a1a67513022b66b99d64255 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mollomm1 <68751598+Mollomm1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:43:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: Add contrast detection autofocus

The rear camera of the Samsung Galaxy Tab A 10.1 (2019, SM-T510) has a
DW9808 voice coil lens, which the kernel exposes as a lens subdevice of
the S5K4HA sensor. The simple pipeline handler cannot drive it, as the
software ISP and IPA know nothing about lenses.

- software_isp: measure the sharpness of the centre half of the image:
  the sum of squared differences between neighbouring boxes of four green
  samples. Box filtering keeps the sensor noise from swamping the
  measure in low light.
- ipa: simple: pass the lens controls to the IPA, and let it send lens
  positions back through a new setLensControls event.
- ipa: simple: add an Af algorithm. It scans the lens from infinity in
  coarse steps until the sharpness has clearly passed its peak, refines
  around the best position, and in continuous mode rescans when the
  sharpness changes at a stable exposure. Gain changes alter the noise
  and so the sharpness, so it measures only while the AGC holds exposure
  and gain, pausing a scan until the AGC settles. It supports AfMode, AfTrigger
  and LensPosition, and reports AfState and LensPosition. Continuous is
  the default mode, as most applications never ask for focus.
- simple: apply the lens positions, and park the lens at its rest
  position when the camera stops, since the voice coil draws current in
  proportion to its position while the lens subdevice stays open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
